  "problem": "Let $x(\\theta )$ and $y(\\theta )$ represent the $x$- and $y$-coordinates of a point on the given curve. Write expressions for $x(\\theta )$ and $y(\\theta )$ in terms of $\\theta .$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x(\\theta )\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y(\\theta )\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use \n\n$x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,$ and $\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$\n\nwhere $x,$ $y,$ and $r$ are functions of $\\theta .$\n\nUsing the fact that $r=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we get \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\ny=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =6{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$",
